{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,360p' /output/blocker_ledger.json; printf '\\\\n### handoff\\\\n'; sed -n '1,360p' /output/analysis_handoff.json; printf '\\\\n### recovery script\\\\n'; sed -n '1,420p' /output/recovery/recovery_attempts.sh; printf '\\\\n### article methods matches\\\\n'; rg -n -i -C 3 'case-crossover|lag 0|three-day|three day|SIM|Mortality Information|conditional|temperature|humidity|Data availability' /study/article.txt | sed -n '1,420p'; printf '\\\\n### source capabilities snippets\\\\n'; rg -n -i -C 2 'SIM|datasus|mortality|Brazil|REDU|Fiocruz' /run/contract/public-source-capabilities.json | sed -n '1,260p'\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"status\": \"blocked\",\n  \"decisive_blocker\": \"No decoded, fit-ready daily all-cancer outcome records were recovered within the run after the official legacy DBC transport timed out and the only verified public substitute health archive could not be safely range-resumed by the available execution transport.\",\n  \"attempts\": [\n    {\"route\":\"Elsevier API / ScienceDirect\",\"result\":\"Crossref exposed the full-text endpoint, but API returned metadata only and ScienceDirect returned Cloudflare application error. Complete article methods were independently recovered from the author-uploaded ResearchGate copy.\"},\n    {\"route\":\"DATASUS official DBC, DOESP2019\",\"result\":\"HTTPS and HTTP connections to ftp.datasus.gov.br timed out after 10 seconds; no bytes recovered.\"},\n    {\"route\":\"OpenDataSUS catalog\",\"result\":\"Portal loaded, but its old CKAN host could not be resolved from this environment.\"},\n    {\"route\":\"REDU Climaterna public Dataverse\",\"result\":\"Catalog, readme, and 61.9-MB pollution archive downloaded and decoded. The 2,779,832,439-byte health archive route was verified, but HTTP Range was ignored; interrupted transfer retries appended duplicate bytes. The retained file was explicitly not decoded or used.\"},\n    {\"route\":\"Counterexample review\",\"result\":\"The Ministry mortality page confirms anonymous SIM microdata exist in DBC and CSV; Climaterna independently confirms an annual Parquet mirror. Neither yielded a usable, decoded cancer-death partition under the active transport constraint. The IVIS mirror was rejected because it contains natural-cause aggregate mortality, not cancer causes.\"}\n  ],\n  \"remaining_action\": \"On a continuation with a durable download session or an annual-file endpoint, start the health archive afresh, verify ZIP integrity, extract one deterministic 2019 annual SIM partition, filter ICD-10 C00-C97 and municipality 3550308, then link to a documented PM2.5 and weather series before fitting.\"\n}\n\n### handoff\n{\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"study_id\": \"38788590-brazil-cancer\",\n  \"status\": \"blocked\",\n  \"fidelity\": \"none\",\n  \"target\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"Daily all-cancer deaths (ICD-10 C00-C97)\",\n    \"pollutant\": \"PM2.5\",\n    \"geography\": \"Brazilian municipalities (5570 in the article)\",\n    \"population\": \"Individual Brazilian Mortality Information System cancer death records\",\n    \"period\": \"2000-01-01 through 2019-12-31\",\n    \"effect_scale\": \"Odds ratio per 10 micrograms per cubic metre\",\n    \"exposure_assignment\": \"Population-weighted municipal mean of 0.25-degree daily PM2.5 grids; lag 0-2 three-day mean\",\n    \"model\": \"Time-stratified case-crossover conditional logistic regression; same weekday within calendar month controls\",\n    \"covariates\": [\"temperature cross-basis\", \"relative humidity\", \"public holiday\"],\n    \"named_outcome_source\": \"Brazilian Mortality Information System (SIM)\",\n    \"specification_evidence\": [\"/study/article.txt\", \"ResearchGate full-text recovery, methods lines 424-790\", \"/output/recovery/pubmed-38788590.medline\"]\n  },\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\"role\":\"outcome\",\"url\":\"https://ftp.datasus.gov.br/dissemin/publicos/SIM/CID10/DADOS/DOESP2019.dbc\",\"route_origin\":\"article_named\",\"retrieved\":false,\"sha256\":null,\"evidence_artifact\":\"/output/recovery/doesp2019.headers\"},\n    {\"role\":\"outcome\",\"url\":\"https://redu.unicamp.br/api/datasets/:persistentId?persistentId=doi:10.25824/redu/ZE4IJM\",\"route_origin\":\"agent_discovered\",\"retrieved\":true,\"sha256\":null,\"evidence_artifact\":\"/output/recovery/climaterna-dataset.json\"},\n    {\"role\":\"exposure\",\"url\":\"https://redu.unicamp.br/api/access/datafile/17719\",\"route_origin\":\"agent_discovered\",\"retrieved\":true,\"sha256\":null,\"evidence_artifact\":\"/output/recovery/cetesb_mp25.parquet\"}\n  ],\n  \"substitutions\": [],\n  \"coverage\": {\n    \"eligible_units\": 5570,\n    \"included_units\": 0,\n    \"eligible_times\": 7305,\n    \"included_times\": 0,\n    \"rule\": \"No rows retained without a decoded, date- and municipality-linkable cancer outcome and covariate-compatible exposure.\",\n    \"notes\": \"No analysis panel was produced; see coverage_diagnostics.json.\"\n  },\n  \"artifacts\": {\n    \"code\": \"/output/recovery/recovery_attempts.sh\",\n    \"source_manifest\": \"/output/source_manifest.json\",\n    \"exposure\": \"/output/recovery/cetesb_mp25.parquet\",\n    \"analysis_panel\": null,\n    \"model_output\": null,\n    \"decision_log\": \"/output/decision_log.json\",\n    \"research_notebook\": \"/output/aeris-workspace/.aeris/research-notebook.json\",\n    \"blocker_ledger\": \"/output/blocker_ledger.json\",\n    \"fidelity_record\": \"/output/aeris-workspace/.aeris/artifacts/reanalysis-fidelity_reanalysis-fidelity_2026-09-26T063735.1888660000.json\",\n    \"coverage_diagnostics\": \"/output/coverage_diagnostics.json\",\n    \"boundary_route_evidence\": \"/output/blocker_ledger.json\",\n    \"study_contract\": \"/output/aeris-workspace/.aeris/contracts/reanalysis-invariants.json\"\n  },\n  \"blockers\": [\n    \"Official DATASUS DBC transport timed out from this environment.\",\n    \"The verified public SIM-compatible REDU health archive could not be safely completed with the available interrupting transfer transport because it ignored Range requests; no decoded outcome records were used.\",\n    \"Without a daily cancer ICD-10 outcome partition, an article-aligned conditional case-crossover fit is not defensible.\"\n  ]\n}\n\n### recovery script\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Executable record of the decisive public-data recovery routes.\nset -euo pipefail\n\n# Article and metadata routes (yielded usable metadata; ResearchGate full text\n# was consulted through the browser because ScienceDirect returned a Cloudflare error).\ncurl -L --fail 'https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/efetch.fcgi?db=pubmed&id=38788590&rettype=medline&retmode=text' -o pubmed-38788590.medline\ncurl -L --fail 'https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1016/j.jhazmat.2024.134606' -o crossref.json\n\n# Official DATASUS legacy transport: failed from this environment (connection timeout).\ncurl -L --connect-timeout 10 --max-time 90 --fail \\\n  'https://ftp.datasus.gov.br/dissemin/publicos/SIM/CID10/DADOS/DOESP2019.dbc' \\\n  -o DOESP2019.dbc\n\n# Verified public substitute catalog and source archive.\ncurl -L --fail 'https://redu.unicamp.br/api/datasets/:persistentId?persistentId=doi:10.25824/redu/ZE4IJM' -o climaterna-dataset.json\ncurl -L --fail 'https://redu.unicamp.br/api/access/datafile/17719' -o pollution.zip\nunzip -p pollution.zip pollution/cetesb_2010_2023_MP2.5.parquet > cetesb_mp25.parquet\n\n# The 2.78-GB health archive is intentionally a resumable transfer. The server\n# did not honor HTTP Range in this run, so retries must start a clean file rather\n# than append with curl -C -. Do not treat the retained partial as decoded data.\ncurl -L --fail --connect-timeout 15 \\\n  'https://redu.unicamp.br/api/access/datafile/17721' -o health.zip\n\n### article methods matches\n21-S0304-3894(24)01185-3\n22-Although some studies have found that short-term PM\n23-2.5\n24:exposure is associated with lung cancer deaths, its impact on other cancer sites is unclear. To answer this research question, this time-stratified case-crossover study used individual cancer death data between January 1, 2000, and December 31, 2019, extracted from the Brazilian mortality information system to quantify the associations between short-term PM\n25-2.5\n26-exposure and cancer mortality from 25 common cancer sites. Daily PM\n27-2.5\n--\n31-3\n32-. For every 10-μg/m\n33-3\n34:increase in three-day average PM\n35-2.5\n36-exposure, the odds ratio (OR) for all-cancer mortality was 1.04 (95% CI 1.03-1.04). Apart from all-cancer deaths, PM\n37-2.5\n\n### source capabilities snippets\n12-    {\n13-      \"source_class\": \"national_health_bulk_files\",\n14:      \"examples\": [\"hospital discharge files\", \"mortality microdata\", \"public tabulations\"],\n15-      \"use\": \"Recover outcome records or aggregate counts from national reporting systems.\",\n16-      \"recovery_patterns\": [\"catalog inspection\", \"legacy file endpoints\", \"bulk-file decoding\", \"successor portals\", \"verified public mirrors\", \"public client source inspection\", \"package catalog or object-store metadata\"],\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
