{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '### current aeris contract' && find /output/aeris-workspace/.aeris/contracts -type f -maxdepth 1 -print -exec sed -n '1,280p' {} \\\\; && printf '%s\\\\n' '### data file summary via jq' && jq -r '.data.latestVersion.files[] | [.dataFile.id,.label,.dataFile.filesize,.dataFile.storageIdentifier] | @tsv' /output/recovery/climaterna-dataset.json && printf '%s\\\\n' '### research README' && sed -n '1,220p' /output/recovery/climaterna-README.md && printf '%s\\\\n' '### sizes' && du -h /output/recovery/* | sort -h | tail -30 && printf '%s\\\\n' '### existing auth outputs' && find /output/aeris-workspace/.aeris -maxdepth 3 -type f -print | sed -n '1,160p'\"","aggregated_output":"### current aeris contract\n/output/aeris-workspace/.aeris/contracts/reanalysis-invariants.json\n{\n  \"schema_version\": \"aeris-study-contract/v3\",\n  \"profile\": \"reanalysis\",\n  \"contract_id\": \"38788590-brazil-cancer-reanalysis-invariants\",\n  \"approved\": true,\n  \"author\": \"agent\",\n  \"objective\": \"What is the association between a 10 \\u00b5g/m\\u00b3 increase in municipality-level three-day mean (lag 0\\u20132) PM2.5 and daily all-cancer mortality in Brazil?\",\n  \"allowed_tools\": [\n    \"estimate_boundary_exposure\",\n    \"estimate_boundary_exposure_batch\",\n    \"estimate_exposure\"\n  ],\n  \"pollutants\": [\n    \"pm25\"\n  ],\n  \"date_window\": {\n    \"start\": \"2000-01-01\",\n    \"end\": \"2019-12-31\"\n  },\n  \"temporal_resolutions\": [\n    \"daily\",\n    \"hourly\"\n  ],\n  \"allowed_fidelity_levels\": [\n    \"matched\",\n    \"source_substitution\",\n    \"reduced_coverage\",\n    \"reduced_adjustment\",\n    \"bounded\",\n    \"supported_sensitivity\"\n  ],\n  \"resource_limits\": {\n    \"wall_clock_hours\": 8,\n    \"maximum_infrastructure_restarts\": 1,\n    \"maximum_single_download_gib\": 10,\n    \"maximum_boundary_units\": 6000,\n    \"maximum_boundary_units_per_call\": 25,\n    \"maximum_static_units_per_call\": 2\n  },\n  \"scientific_invariants\": {\n    \"research_question\": \"What is the association between a 10 \\u00b5g/m\\u00b3 increase in municipality-level three-day mean (lag 0\\u20132) PM2.5 and daily all-cancer mortality in Brazil?\",\n    \"target_outcome_and_population\": \"Daily all-cancer deaths among individual cancer death records registered in Brazil's Mortality Information System across Brazilian municipalities.\",\n    \"pollutants\": [\n      \"pm25\"\n    ],\n    \"principal_contrast\": \"Odds ratio per 10 \\u00b5g/m\\u00b3 increase in three-day mean PM2.5 (lag 0\\u20132).\",\n    \"principal_variants\": [\n      \"All-cancer mortality; site-specific cancer mortality for 25 common sites\"\n    ],\n    \"broad_geography\": \"Brazilian municipalities, Brazil\",\n    \"target_geographic_units\": null,\n    \"target_geographic_unit_type\": \"municipality\",\n    \"period\": {\n      \"start\": \"2000-01-01\",\n      \"end\": \"2019-12-31\"\n    },\n    \"prohibited_evidence\": [\n      \"Published effect estimates\",\n      \"Published exposure values\",\n      \"Prior AERIS effects, code, or source manifests\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"article_evidence\": [\n    {\n      \"artifact\": \"research-notebook_research-notebook_2026-09-26T062426.8509660000\",\n      \"finding\": \"The saved notebook records abstract evidence from /study/article.txt: the study is nationwide Brazil, covers 2000\\u20132019, uses municipality-level daily PM2.5, individual cancer deaths, and reports a three-day PM2.5 contrast.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"artifact\": \"research-notebook_research-notebook_2026-09-26T062426.8509660000\",\n      \"finding\": \"The saved notebook records the supplied study target\\u2019s conditional regression and adjustment variables as provisional details requiring method-route verification.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"article_evidence_map\": {\n    \"supplied_materials\": \"Abstract available in /study/article.txt (lines 22\\u201346); supplied PDF/XML do not contain full methods or supplements.\",\n    \"provisional_target_check\": \"The contract target agrees with the abstract on population, period, geography, pollutant, municipality aggregation, lag 0\\u20132 construct, and per-10 \\u00b5g/m\\u00b3 contrast. Conditional regression and covariates are explicitly tracked for external method verification.\"\n  },\n  \"execution_design\": {},\n  \"amendments\": []\n}\n### data file summary via jq\n17718\tcities_geocodes.csv\t371105\ts3://redu:197aeb3bdf1-9a8577faad3d\n17720\tclimate.zip\t2433637149\ts3://redu:197aecf02f0-0b217dbfb950\n17721\thealth.zip\t2779832439\ts3://redu:197aed711d1-dd0aa9208640\n17719\tpollution.zip\t61861647\ts3://redu:197aeb693fd-c8fb9fa1fde5\n17717\tREADME.md\t3554\ts3://redu:197aeb0d3b4-edaddf0cf998\n### research README\n**Climaterna** provides a comprehensive dataset integrating public data from validated sources, including the Mortality Information System (SIM) and the Live Births Information System (SINASC) of DATASUS, the Brazilian Daily Weather Gridded Data (BR-DWGD), and pollution data from the CMIP6 platform. The dataset comprises anonymized microdata on all births and deaths across Brazilian municipalities, with daily granularity from 2010 to 2022. It also includes annual climate and pollution data for the same period and geographic scope. This integrated dataset enables diverse analyses exploring the relationships between health and environmental variables, particularly focusing on Brazil's maternal and neonatal health outcomes. By combining data from officially validated sources, this dataset supports robust research in epidemiology, public health, and environmental sciences. Furthermore, it can support journalistic reporting and be a reliable resource for anyone interested in cross-referencing climate, health, and pollution data.\n\n::: info\nAll the data is available in **parquet** (tabular) format, enabling efficient access and processing capabilities. **The linkage among files is given by city identifiers, which share consistent values across the datasets**. For SIM and SINASC data, the city ID is the field CODMUNRES. For climate and pollution, the city code is the CODE_MUNI field. Additionally, the file cities_geocodes.csv contains these codes as 'geocodigo' (discarding the last digit) along with their latitude and longitude.\n\n:::\n\n::: success\nAll datasets have summaries (markdown) and complete (PDF) documentation about their data collection protocol and their variable descriptions inside respective folders. \n\n:::\n\n# Climate Data Documentation\n\nThe climate data documentation is available [HERE](https://unidrive.unicamp.br/index.php/s/sXHKbdgtjzR8meQ).\n\n# Health Data Documentation\n\nThe health data documentation is available [HERE](https://unidrive.unicamp.br/index.php/s/Cw3MHrbWZFTiqAp). \n\n# Pollution Data Documentation\n\nThe health data documentation is available [HERE](https://unidrive.unicamp.br/index.php/s/4MYpFzW3tzPC2DJ).\n\n::: info\n***How to cite Climaterna?***  \n  \nIf you use data, models, or tools developed by the Climaterna project in your research or publications, please cite the project as follows:\n\n**ABNT Style** SOARES, Camila Ferreira; de FRANÇA, Breno Bernard Nicolau; COLTRI, Priscila Pereira; LIMA, Everton Emanuel Campos de; TOREZZAN, Cristiano; XAVIER, Alexandre Candido; NICHI, Jaqueline; ALVARADO, Negli René Gallardo; CHARLES, Charles M'poca; SALES, Sergio Floquet; MOTTA, Gabriel Moreira; ANDRADE, Matheus Alves de; RISSO, Mateus Samuel; PEREIRA, Malcolm dos Reis Alves; TORRES, Guilherme Almussa Leite; HYSLOP, Kevin; SILVA, Dimitri de Oliveira; AWE, Oluwafunmilola Deborah; ARANTES, Caio Simplicio; ANDRADE JÚNIOR, Valter Lacerda de; PACAGNELLA, Rodolfo de Carvalho. Climaterna. 2024. Available at: <https://doi.org/10.25824/redu/ZE4IJM>. Accessed on: [insert date]. Research Data Repository of Unicamp, V1.\n\n**Vancouver Style** Soares CF, de França BBN, Coltri PP, Lima EEC, Torezzan C, Xavier AC, Nichi J, Alvarado NRG, Charles CM, Sales SF, Motta GM, Andrade MA, Risso MS, Pereira MRA, Torres GAL, Hyslop K, Silva DO, Awe OD, Arantes CS, Andrade Júnior VL, Pacagnella RC. Climaterna. 2024. Available from: <https://doi.org/10.25824/redu/ZE4IJM>. Research Data Repository of Unicamp, V1. Accessed on: [insert date].\n\nThank you for citing Climaterna and supporting open science!\n\n:::\n\n# ### sizes\n4.0K\t/output/recovery/pubmed.headers\n4.0K\t/output/recovery/recovery_attempts.sh\n4.0K\t/output/recovery/tabnet.headers\n4.0K\t/output/recovery/unpaywall.headers\n8.0K\t/output/recovery/pollution-documentation.md\n8.0K\t/output/recovery/pubmed-38788590.medline\n8.0K\t/output/recovery/unpaywall.json\n20K\t/output/recovery/climaterna-dataset.json\n24K\t/output/recovery/crossref.json\n32K\t/output/recovery/fiocruz.html\n36K\t/output/recovery/58474bfb-df03edda04ff76ba.js\n36K\t/output/recovery/738-03c225b95207c246.js\n36K\t/output/recovery/865-4faca17231494b91.js\n36K\t/output/recovery/_app-effcb7e1acff0518.js\n36K\t/output/recovery/_buildManifest.js\n36K\t/output/recovery/_ssgManifest.js\n36K\t/output/recovery/framework-64a2550aaa69836a.js\n36K\t/output/recovery/index-453ebf556ac33707.js\n36K\t/output/recovery/main-78871ba9036653a9.js\n36K\t/output/recovery/opendatasus-mortality.html\n36K\t/output/recovery/opendatasus.json\n36K\t/output/recovery/polyfills-42372ed130431b0a.js\n36K\t/output/recovery/webpack-6f363cd1990801ba.js\n120K\t/output/recovery/climaterna.xml\n128K\t/output/recovery/tabnet.html\n256K\t/output/recovery/health-tail.bin\n816K\t/output/recovery/elsevier.html\n3.8M\t/output/recovery/cetesb_mp25.parquet\n60M\t/output/recovery/pollution.zip\n3.5G\t/output/recovery/health.zip\n### existing auth outputs\n/output/aeris-workspace/.aeris/artifacts/research-notebook_research-notebook_2026-09-26T062426.8509660000.manifest.json\n/output/aeris-workspace/.aeris/artifacts/research-notebook_research-n