in NetCDF format from the IPSL-CM5A2-INCA, EC-Earth3-AerChem, GFDL-ESM4, MPI-ESM-1-2-HAM models. The data was processed and interpolated to Brazil's municipal boundaries using *Python* (*numpy*, *xarray*, *pandas*, *geopandas*, and *regionmask* libraries). The daily measurements of the different elements were aggregated to monthly averages using specialized functions developed for this purpose.\n\n## Data Description\n\nThe pollution dataset was created with the variables of the Molar Fraction of Particulate Materials in the Air. Table 3 lists the materials selected to make up the pollution dataset.\n\nThe chemical elements were selected based on the pollutant analysis data table of the São Paulo State Environmental Company (CETESB). CETESB is a reference institution for monitoring and controlling air quality in Brazil. It carries out regular measurements of various atmospheric pollutants, such as CO, NO2, SO2, and O3, providing essential data for understanding the impact of pollution on the environment and public health. Monitoring the variables collected by CETESB is crucial for supporting environmental policies and health studies and assessing the effectiveness of pollution mitigation measures.\n\n**Table 3.** Characteristics of CMIP-6 pollution databases.\n\n| **Model**             | **Variable** | **Experiment** | **Frequency** | **Period (m/y)**      | **Units**     | **Description**                                                              |\n|-------------------|----------|------------|-----------|-------------------|-----------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| IPSL-CM5A2-INCA   | c2h6     | Historical | Monthly   | 01/1950 - 12/2014 | mol mol-1 | Mixing ratio of C2H6 volume in air                                       |\n| IPSL-CM5A2-INCA   | c2h6     | Ssp370     | Monthly   | 01/2015 - 12/2055 | mol mol-1 | Mixing ratio of C2H6 volume in air                                       |\n| IPSL-CM5A2-INCA   | ch3